ARRAY: 
datatype arr_name[size]
eg: marks
int marks[5]
memory = no. of elements(size) * size of datatype
memory = 5 * 4
memory= 20 bytes, 160 bits

- int, float - 4 bytes
- char 1 byte
- double - 8 bytes
- 1 byte - 8 bits

- In array indexing always starts from 0.
eg: arr[5] = 0 to 4

- array stores in continuous memory.

- To initialize multiple elements in array
arr[5] = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}.


